tion the rifle is held, and the amount and number of doubles shot. Like trap shooting, it is shot with a shotgun. The other six events in 1968 were the same as in 1960-64 – two pistol events, three rifle events, and trap shooting. All the shooting events were held at the " [:a {:href "/venues/496"} "Vincente Suárez Shooting Range"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The other big change in 1968 Olympic shooting was that women were allowed to compete for the first time, shooting alongside the men. Three women competed – " [:a {:href "/athletes/43686"} "Eulalia Rolińska"] " (POL) in prone small-bore rifle, finishing 22nd, " [:a {:href "/athletes/43610"} "Gladys de Seminario"] " (PER) in prone small-bore rifle, finishing 31st; and " [:a {:href "/athletes/43291"} "Nuria Ortíz"] " (MEX) in skeet shooting, placing 13th."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51708"} "Rapid-Fire Pistol, 25 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "22 – 23 October 1968"] "\n" [:td {} "56"] "\n" [:td {} "34"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51709"} "Free Pistol, 50 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "18 October 1968"] "\n" [:td {} "69"] "\n" [:td {} "42"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51716"} "Free Rifle, Three Positions, 300 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 October 1968"] "\n" [:td {} "30"] "\n" [:td {} "16"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51712"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Three Positions, 50 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "21 October 1968"] "\n" [:td {} "62"] "\n" [:td {} "35"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51711"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Prone, 50 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "19